# NOTE FOR ANYONE ADDING ZENODO METADATA LATER.
# Zenodo reads this file when archiving a GitHub release, BUT if a .zenodo.json is also present it
# uses that and ignores this file silently. Do not add a .zenodo.json alongside this one unless you
# intend it to be the single source of truth, or a minted DOI will carry whichever metadata is
# stale. This repository deliberately keeps CITATION.cff only.
cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SwarmInfluence-Bench"
message: "If you use this work, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Jacob
    given-names: Manu Nicholas
    email: manunicholasjacob@gmail.com
    affiliation: Independent Researcher
abstract: >-
  A benchmark for coordination and influence detectors on multi-agent chat, in which the true
  influence graph is known by construction. Includes pure nulls, which measure calibration, and
  common-cause nulls, which measure confounding.
keywords:
  - transfer entropy
  - multi-agent systems
  - AI safety
  - surrogate data
  - coordination detection
license: MIT
version: 0.2.0
date-released: "2026-11-06"
repository-code: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/swarm-influence-bench"
url: "https://github.com/manunicholasjacob/swarm-influence-bench"
